<h2>Does MCP work with Codex as reliably as Claude Code and Cursor?</h2>
<p class="answer">Yes: Codex connects to roughly the same set of reference and npm MCP servers as Claude Code, Cursor, Grok Build and Pi when tested on identical server commands.</p>
[[SMX:MCP_BY_AGENT_TABLE]]
<p>In our Nov 20, 2026 baseline (<code>testing/results/2026-11-20.json</code>), Codex passed 8 of 9 reference MCP servers (88.9%) and 22 of 45 npm MCP servers (48.9%), right alongside Cursor (9/9 and 23/45) and Claude Code (8/9 and 20/45). Because Codex's CLI has no standalone MCP health check without signing in, our harness verifies Codex registers the server as enabled and then performs the exact MCP <code>initialize</code> + <code>tools/list</code> handshake using the command Codex would launch (<a href="/how-we-test/">see full methodology</a>).</p>

